==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Seaside Pegasa, type v''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Seaside Pegasa is a very decent crowd-controller against her target traits, moreso than the original [[Pegasa (Uber Rare Cat)|Pegasa]]! She has an amazing standing range, with a [[Weaken]] uptime of 72.3% to 84.9% to enemies in her range, and an impressive maximum range of 732.5 thanks to her [[Mini-Wave]]. Her matchups are equally as impressive, comfortably outranging a majority of enemies within her targets, including even backliners like [[Master A.]] and [[THE SLOTH]]. Additionally, Weaken works wonders against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]], whose most notable threats all have immensely high DPS and pushing power ([[R.Ost]], [[H. Nah]], [[Dark Otter]], [[Bun Bun Black]], etc.).

[[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] is also very useful for handling Traitless enemies like [[Kory]], [[Dober P.D]] and [[Mr. Mer]], as well as [[Two Can]] for Dark enemies and is also just generally helpful for mixed stages. Her [[Conjure]] provides a very powerful safety net that [[Slow|Slows]] enemies for a monstrous '''6 seconds''' whenever you're in a bind, while also dealing a hefty amount of damage. She has a high knockback count and effective HP through Weaken, meaning you don't have to worry about her dying all too often either.

But despite her strengths, the damage output she provides on her own is rather underwhelming, and she is highly vulnerable to any form of status effect from gimmicky enemies like [[Croakley]] or [[Henry]]. Regardless, Seaside Pegasa is a good unit to own for crowned [[Legend Stages]], where enemy magnifications reach blatantly unfair levels, especially against the stat-focused [[Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] type.

